{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792869631,"nonce":"3GCZFd1p3A0xlXaaAwk/XHNqwXw=","title":"TypeScript: instance get and set accessors","message":"58 official rows stopped at accessors. An instance accessor is a pair of methods: reading the property calls the getter and assigning calls the setter, each dispatched on the instance's class like methods, and the assignment's value is the assigned value. Checked as TypeScript does: assigning a getter-only property (2540), a getter that returns no value (2378), accessors duplicating fields or methods (2300), and visibility of overriding accessors (2415). Unsupported: static accessors, compound assignments and updates through accessors, reading an accessor without a getter, accessors overriding fields or methods and fields overriding accessors (whose meaning depends on the class field semantics), setter parameters typed by the getter, and structural use of class instances with accessors where a record view needs fields.","files":null}]}